
// draft
locate(verdicts: Bool[]) -> Int[]
	note "yield the index of each position at which pred returned true, where verdicts is pred's answer on each item, or on each window when window_size is given, in order"
	# Every output index is a position in verdicts at which the verdict is true.
	all i in out: true in verdicts[i .. i + 1]
	# Every position in verdicts at which the verdict is true is in the output.
	// reaching for: a range over the positions of verdicts, 0 up to len(verdicts) - 1 (or the
	// position of a binder's occurrence as an Int), so the line could say: all p in positions of
	// verdicts where true in verdicts[p .. p + 1]: p in out
	# The output is sorted ascending.
	all a in out: all b in out where a before b in out: a <= b
	# No two output indexes are equal.
	unique out
	// example wanted: verdicts empty; no position exists, so nothing can be located
	// example wanted: verdicts all false; no position holds a true verdict
	// example wanted: verdicts all true; every position from 0 to the last is located
	// example wanted: the docstring's [0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0] under bool, as verdicts [false, true,
	// true, false, true, false, false]; positions are counted from 0
	// example wanted: the docstring's window case, 12 items with window_size 3, as one verdict per
	// window starting at each position, true where the window is (1, 2, 3); the index is the
	// window's starting position
